at the World Economic Forum this year  there has been much talk about economic  justice for some the German Finance  Minister Wolfgang schäuble doesn't  really fit this mold he has helped many  countries in the EU zone to pass painful  reforms and that has often led to him  being accused of lacking solidarity in a  conversation with DW director-general  Peter Limbach Shora had to defend  himself  solidarity doesn't mean constantly  handing out money you don't have  that's called occurring debts rather  solidarity means solving problems and  constantly justifying your solutions  Charlotte believes austerity is the only  way that countries like Spain will once  again be able to borrow and he believes  austerity is the only way to maintain  the confidence of the market Europe  doesn't have to become Germany but it  has to remain strong if it wants to have  a place in a globalized world it can't  put its relatively high social security  bill if it can't maintain a basic level  of economic competitiveness and Minda  standard on victory of spearhead of 32  country but everyone at the Davos  conference is interested about how  things will develop in the future not  just the Europeans in today's globalized  world the success or failures of large  economic bloc's such as Europe have  global knock-on effects
 

